---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactBlock from '../../components/ContactBlock.astro';

// The thesis: the name taken literally, then ten propositions.
// It names no project or programme, so it does not date when those change.
// This page is about the ideas. What is sold is on the home, work and method pages.
const theses: { n: string; title: string; body: string[] }[] = [
  { n: 'I', title: 'Somebody rules.', body: [
    'Every household, company and country is governed by someone or something: one person’s memory, a vendor’s terms, or a structure built on purpose. The open matter is never whether, only how well.',
    'The demand for good rule is unlimited and permanent. Every civilisation that built anything lasting built it on this.',
  ] },
  { n: 'II', title: 'Good rule is scarce.', body: [
    'It is the exercise of judgment, responsibility and care by people able to see reality clearly, act on what they see, and accept the obligations that come with the power they hold.',
    'That capacity does not arise by itself. Management and administration are downstream of it.',
  ] },
  { n: 'III', title: 'It does not maintain itself.', body: [
    'Prohibitions do not enforce themselves. Principles do not persist without structures that carry them. Even restraint has to be actively enacted.',
    'When the chain of transmission breaks, what follows is consistent: procedure in place of authority, and obligation that runs one way only.',
  ] },
  { n: 'IV', title: 'What persists is structure.', body: [
    'People leave. What they built into a structure stays. It keeps its function through time, survives the departure of individuals, resists degradation under pressure, and passes its principles to those who come after.',
    'Building these structures is the work.',
  ] },
  { n: 'V', title: 'See first.', body: [
    'The state of affairs has to be seen clearly before any work begins: what is true, what is reciprocal, what will survive contact with human nature.',
  ] },
  { n: 'VI', title: 'Advance, or oscillate.', body: [
    'A structure driven by problems moves until the problem recedes, and then stops. A structure held between an honest account of what is and a clear picture of what is wanted resolves forward.',
    'The path is structural, not motivational.',
  ] },
  { n: 'VII', title: 'Reciprocity holds it together.', body: [
    'Reputation, credit, obligation and trust all circulate. Designing how they flow is designing the circulatory system of good rule.',
    'A structure in which duty runs in both directions holds. This work is not for those who seek to extract without reciprocating.',
  ] },
  { n: 'VIII', title: 'The ground has moved.', body: [
    'The structures built for the twentieth century cannot withstand or steer what is happening now. Every workflow, role and form of cooperation is being reorganised around AI.',
    'Whether you wield these tools to create outcomes or consume products controlled by others is a difference in sovereignty.',
  ] },
  { n: 'IX', title: 'Sovereignty is built.', body: [
    'Self-determination by self-determined means. In practice: parts you own, people you are bound to by mutual obligation, and the capacity to process information correctly and act on it quickly.',
  ] },
  { n: 'X', title: 'A tradition is a structure that teaches.', body: [
    'It is alive when it is practised by people who understand its function, and it lasts when each person who does the work becomes able to carry it.',
    'This one is young. This is the craft. This is statecraft.',
  ] },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Thesis" description="Ten propositions on good rule: it is scarce, it does not maintain itself, and it endures only through structures built to carry it.">
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>Ten propositions on good rule.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Why the practice exists and what its name means. Statecraft is the craft of good rule.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section flush" aria-label="The name">
    <ul class="defs">
      <li class="reveal">
        <h2 class="w">State</h2>
        <p>The unit that must be governed. The condition a system is in. The state of affairs, which has to be seen clearly before any work begins.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="reveal">
        <h2 class="w">Craft</h2>
        <p>Direct contact with the material. Honest assessment, skilled making, the hand on the work.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="reveal">
        <h2 class="w">Systems</h2>
        <p>What remains after individuals leave. What compounds. What holds an obligation in place when nobody is watching.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <ol class="wrap theses">
    {theses.map((t) => (
      <li class="reveal">
        <span class="n">{t.n}</span>
        <h2>{t.title}</h2>
        {t.body.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <section class="wrap after-list">
    <a class="btn ghost" href="/disciplines">The four disciplines</a>
  </section>

  <ContactBlock />
</BaseLayout>
